ing and thus defrauding sam crowe  of money based on the mortal compass he  presents throughout the rest of the show  we'd expect bobby to turn luanne in to  face the consequences of her actions by  my calculations  you've been cutting us light for six  years  instead he gives in to her advances and  chooses not to disclose her theft  it's a decision that doesn't make sense  given bobby's tendency to do what's best  for the club  luanne is otto delaney's old lady  despite the fact that the prison clause  we're still not sure if that's actually  a thing in real life mc culture but we  hope not allows other members to have  relations with an old lady while her man  is in prison it's just wrong on so many  levels and not really in keeping with  the character as a whole  season 4 has a 100 critic score on  rotten tomatoes a peculiar score  considering there's a major issue with  the finale assistant u.s attorney  lincoln potter rolls into town as  members of sam crowe are released from  prison and recruits eli roosevelt the  new top dog at the san joaquin county  sheriff department to be a part of his  multi-agency task force to bring down  sam crowe the true ira and russian  organized crime all in one fell swoop  potter sows dissension in the ranks by  forcing jews to betray his club in order  to remain a member when he and roosevelt  convinced the wayward juan carlos to  steal a brick of cocaine sam crowe got  from the galindo cartel represented by  romero romeo perata and luis torres  potter is an antagonist who's ambitious  and cunning to boot in fact he's so good  that it looks like he's got all his  ducks in a row and is about to clear the  board with a massive rico case then the  cartel shows up to make that all go away  see parata and torres are actually  members of the cia working on a black  book operation and the american  government is backing the galindo cartel  in the hopes of putting other cartels  out of business and eliminating the  violence between the